    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense, the resource gap is definitely a huge part of it. But some people argue that even when you control for money and school funding, those gaps still persist in the data. Do you think there are other underlying factors at play, maybe related to cultural emphasis on certain types of learning or even biological differences in cognitive development that contribute to the variation?",
